" \\\\\n  -p 4.2: \\\"Verify the future behavior with a static source review and one browser user story that clicks the current last button through the fourth generated button and observes the finished state.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$plan_dir\" scope '\"\\\\\n  -p 5.1: \\\"In scope: planning the future creation of button-chain.html, its initial button, generated-button append behavior, fourth-generated-button completion behavior, visible white border styling, manual/static verification, and browser UI-story verification.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 5.2: \\\"Out of scope for this proof: creating button-chain.html now, editing any HTML now, launching a browser or server now, using console shortcuts for UI proof, adding dependencies, or changing repository files outside this plan directory and session-id.txt.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$plan_dir\" affected-areas '\"\\\\\n  -p 6.1: \\\"Future affected file: button-chain.html. Planned DOM scope: body button chain and completion message. Planned style scopes: button layout and .completion-message. Planned script scopes: appendNextButton(), completeDocument(), and the click handler for the current last button.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 6.2: \\\"No backend, build system, package manager, database, or server configuration is expected for the future task.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --description-section \"$plan_dir\" constraints-and-decisions '\"\\\\\n  -p 7.1: \\\"Use only plain HTML, CSS, and JavaScript in the future file unless the executor discovers a repository convention requiring otherwise. The fourth generated button means the fourth button appended after the initial button, not the initial button itself.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 7.2: \\\"The last button rule is strict: only clicking the current last button may append exactly one new button below it; older buttons must not append more butt