{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'set -e\nexport PLANS_ROOT=/tmp/current-fresh7/current/workspace\nPLANNING_SKILL_DIR=/tmp/ai-skills-capsules/20260811T123516Z-current-fresh7/current/worker/planning\nplan_dir=basic-test-proof-current-20260811T123516Z-current-fresh7-isolated-plan\nu=\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\"\n\"$u\" --goal-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain current-state-and-prior-goal-handoffs -p 2.1: \"No implementation file exists during this planning proof. The future executor starts from the plan contract and creates button-chain.html only during the implementation task.\"\n\"$u\" --goal-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain why-this-goal-is-needed -p 4.1: \"This goal creates the entire future runtime surface: the initial control, generated-button chain, completion transition, and visible completion styling. Without it, the UI story has no valid target.\"\n\"$u\" --goal-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain scope -p 5.1: \"In scope: one new button-chain.html file containing the markup, style, and script needed for the specified behavior.\" -p 5.2: \"Out of scope: browser execution, server setup, external libraries, persistence, animation, or additional UI beyond what is necessary to satisfy the button-chain contract.\"\n\"$u\" --goal-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain affected-areas -p 6.1: \"File: button-chain.html. Markup scope: body button-chain-root. Style scope: .completion-message. Script scopes: appendNextButton() and completeDocument().\"\n\"$u\" --goal-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain dependencies-and-handoffs -p 7.1: \"This goal has no prior-goal dependency. It hands button-chain.html and the static contract review result to 02-validate-button-chain.\"\n\"$u\" --goal-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain implementation-approach-risks-and-edge-cases -p 8.1: \"Use a generatedCount value initialized to 0. The initial button click should call the append logic for generated button 1. Each appended button receives the next generated number and becomes the only button allowed to continue the chain.\" -p 8.2: \"When generatedCount reaches 4 and that fourth generated button is clicked, clear document.body or the root container and render a completion element containing exactly finished with a visible white border.\"\n\"$u\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain 11.1 \"Not applicable; this goal owns five work units, within the 2-10 work-unit limit.\"\n\"$u\" --goal-section \"$plan_dir\" 02-validate-button-chain current-state-and-prior-goal-handoffs -p 2.1: \"This goal starts after 01-build-button-chain has created button-chain.html and W05 has confirmed the static contract. No browser proof exists before this goal.\"\n\"$u\" --goal-section \"$plan_dir\" 02-validate-button-chain why-this-goal-is-needed -p 4.1: \"The requested behavior is interactive, so final acceptance requires direct browser clicks that prove the current-last-button rule and the fourth-generated completion state in the rendered UI.\"\n\"$u\" --goal-section \"$plan_dir\" 02-validate-button-chain scope -p 5.1: \"In scope: one browser UI story, US-01, using direct mouse clicks on the visible current last button and recording pass/fail evidence in the story run cache.\" -p 5.2: \"Out of scope: console-triggered events, JavaScript evaluation shortcuts, storage edits, API requests, or changing implementation while running the verification step.\"\n\"$u\" --goal-section \"$plan_dir\" 02-validate-button-chain affected-areas -p 6.1: \"Verification target: implemented local button-chain.html opened by the executor in a browser. Plan artifacts updated by the executor after the run: ui-user-stories.md, ui-story-runs/US-01.md, bugs.md if a bug is found, and progress trackers.\"\n\"$u\" --goal-section \"$plan_dir\" 02-validate-button-chain dependencies-and-handoffs -p 7.1: \"Depends on W01 through W05. Handoff at completion is the recorded browser evidence that US-01 passed and no unresolved bug register entries remain.\"\n\"$u\" --goal-section \"$plan_dir\" 02-validate-button-chain implementation-approach-risks-and-edge-cases -p 8.1: \"Open the completed file in a browser, click only the visible current last button, and after each click wait for the next visible button or final completion state. Stop and open a bug-register entry if the page appends more than one button, appends from a stale button, clears too early, fails to clear on generated button 4, or omits the exact bordered finished state.\"\n\"$u\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 02-validate-button-chain 11.1 \"Allowed single-work-unit exception: this goal is a standalone verification outcome that owns exactly one browser-story verification unit.\"\n# Step sections\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain/01-step-markup instructions -p 5.1: \"Create button-chain.html with valid HTML document structure, a body-level root for the button chain, and exactly one initial button visible when the page first loads.\" -p 5.2: \"Do not add generated buttons in the initial markup. Generated buttons must be created only by the script behavior in W03.\"\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain/01-step-markup acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"Source review shows exactly one initial button in the starting markup and a stable root or body scope where generated buttons can be appended below the current last button.\"\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain/01-step-markup handoff -p 7.1: \"W02 can style the completion state and W03 can attach behavior to the initial button without changing the initial markup contract.\"\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain/02-step-completion-style instructions -p 5.1: \"Add CSS for .completion-message that makes the completion text visibly bordered in white. The border must be visible against the chosen page background.\" -p 5.2: \"Keep the style local to button-chain.html and avoid hiding, clipping, or transforming the exact completion text.\"\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain/02-step-completion-style acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"Source review shows .completion-message has a white border declaration or equivalent visible white border treatment, with enough padding or layout for the border to be seen.\"\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain/02-step-completion-style handoff -p 7.1: \"W04 can render the completion element with class completion-message and rely on the visible white border styling.\"\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain/03-step-append-behavior instructions -p 5.1: \"Implement appendNextButton() so clicking the current last button appends exactly one new generated button below it.\" -p 5.2: \"After appending, make the new generated button the current last button. Older buttons must not append additional buttons once they are no longer the last button.\"\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain/03-step-append-behavior acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"Source review shows a single append path per valid click, generatedCount increments by one per append, and stale buttons cannot continue appending after a newer last button exists.\"\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain/03-step-append-behavior handoff -p 7.1: \"W04 can rely on generatedCount or equivalent state to identify when the fourth generated button has been reached.\"\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain/04-step-completion-behavior instructions -p 5.1: \"Implement completeDocument() and the fourth-generated-button branch so pressing generated button 4 clears the document content and renders the completion state.\" -p 5.2: \"The completion state must contain the exact lowercase text finished and the element carrying that text must use the visible white border style from W02.\"\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain/04-step-completion-behavior acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"Source review shows the completion branch is tied to generated button number 4, not the initial button, and that the prior button chain is removed before rendering finished.\"\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain/04-step-completion-behavior handoff -p 7.1: \"W05 can inspect the completed source for the full contract and W06 can verify it through browser clicks.\"\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain/05-step-static-contract-review instructions -p 5.1: \"After W01-W04 are implemented, inspect button-chain.html source without running it. Check the markup, style, and script against every acceptance criterion in W01-W04.\" -p 5.2: \"Record any mismatch as a blocker for the owning work unit; do not alter code inside this verification step.\"\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain/05-step-static-contract-review acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"The review confirms one initial button, no pre-rendered generated buttons, exactly-one append logic for the current last button, fourth-generated completion, exact finished text, and visible white border styling.\"\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain/05-step-static-contract-review handoff -p 7.1: \"If static review passes, 02-validate-button-chain may proceed to browser UI-story validation. If it fails, return to the specific owning implementation work unit.\"\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 02-validate-button-chain/01-step-browser-story-us-01 instructions -p 5.1: \"Open the implemented local button-chain.html in a browser. Use only direct mouse clicks on the visible current last button: initial button, generated button 1, generated button 2, generated button 3, generated button 4.\" -p 5.2: \"After each click before completion, confirm exactly one new button appears below the previous last button. After clicking generated button 4, confirm the prior document content is cleared and the page shows exactly finished with a visible white border.\"\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 02-validate-button-chain/01-step-browser-story-us-01 acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"US-01 is marked passed only when the browser evidence shows the exact click sequence, exactly-one append after each eligible click, no stale-button append path, clearing on generated button 4, and bordered lowercase finished text.\" -p 6.2: \"If any condition fails, mark US-01 bug found, add a bug row with reproduction and evidence, and create investigation/fix work units before retesting.\"\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 02-validate-button-chain/01-step-browser-story-us-01 handoff -p 7.1: \"Completion handoff is the updated ui-story-runs/US-01.md evidence, updated ui-user-stories.md status, clear bugs.md state, and completed progress trackers.\"\n# Testing companions\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/create-step-testing.sh\" \"$plan_dir/01-build-button-chain\" 01-step-markup \"Static verification: inspect button-chain.html after implementation and confirm the initial DOM contains exactly one visible initial button and no generated buttons. Browser verification is covered downstream by W06/US-01.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/create-step-testing.sh\" \"$plan_dir/01-build-button-chain\" 02-step-completion-style \"Static verification: inspect button-chain.html after implementation and confirm .completion-message or the equivalent completion element has a visible white border treatment. Browser verification is covered downstream by W06/US-01.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/create-step-testing.sh\" \"$plan_dir/01-build-button-chain\" 03-step-append-behavior \"Static verification: inspect the append logic and confirm one generated button is appended per valid current-last-button click, generated count advances once, and stale buttons cannot keep appending. Browser verification is covered downstream by W06/US-01.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/create-step-testing.sh\" \"$plan_dir/01-build-button-chain\" 04-step-completion-behavior \"Static verification: inspect the completion branch and confirm generated button 4 clears prior content and renders exact lowercase finished using the visible white border style. Browser verification is covered downstream by W06/US-01.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/create-step-testing.sh\" \"$plan_dir/01-build-button-chain\" 05-step-static-contract-review \"Verification record: document the source-review result in the step handoff or working context. Pass only if all W01-W04 source contracts are satisfied; otherwise return to the owning step without changing code here.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/create-step-testing.sh\" \"$plan_dir/02-validate-button-chain\" 01-step-browser-story-us-01 \"Browser verification: run US-01 from ui-story-runs/US-01.md using direct clicks only. Expected result is exact lowercase finished with a visible white border after generated button 4, with no unresolved bug rows.\"\nfind \"$plan_dir\" -maxdepth 3 -type f | sort'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
