 the visible initial button; the second click is intentionally on a stale non-last button and uses no console, injected events, storage edits, or API shortcuts.\" \"The stale initial-button click does not append any additional button; generated button 1 remains the current last button and the user can continue US-01 from the valid current-last control.\" W03,W07,W08\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/configure-ui-story-cache.sh\" \"$plan_dir\" US-02 \"Implemented button-chain.html opened from the local workspace in a browser with a clean document state.\" \"Mouse click initial button to append generated button 1; mouse click the original initial button again while it is no longer last.\" \"Original initial button after generated button 1 exists.\" \"Button count remains unchanged after the stale click; no generated button 2 appears until generated button 1 is clicked.\" \"2 seconds after the stale click to confirm no append occurs.\"\n# Update plan and goals for new units\n\"$u\" --description-section \"$plan_dir\" affected-areas '\"\\\\\n  -p 6.1: \\\"Future affected file: button-chain.html. Planned DOM scope: body button-chain-root. Planned style scopes: .button-chain vertical layout and .completion-message visible white border. Planned script scopes: appendNextButton(), completeDocument(), and the click handler for the current last button.\\\" \\\\\n  -p 6.2: \\\"No backend, build system, package manager, database, or server configuration is expected for the future task.\\\"\n\\\"\"'$u\" --goal-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain affected-areas -p 6.1: \"File: button-chain.html. Markup scope: body button-chain-root. Style scopes: .button-chain and .completion-message. Script scopes: appendNextButton() and completeDocument().\"\n\"$u\" --goal-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain dependencies-and-handoffs -p 7.1: \"This goal has no prior-goal dependency. It hands button-chain.html, the vertical button-chain layout, and the static contract review result to 02-validate-button-chain.\"\n\"$u\" --goal-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain implementation-approach-risks-and-edge-cases -p 8.1: \"Use a generatedCount value initialized to 0. The initial button click should call the append logic for generated button 1. Each appended button receives the next generated number and becomes the only button allowed to continue the chain.\" -p 8.2: \"Lay out the chain with a vertical container or block-level buttons so every appended button appears below the previous last button.\" -p 8.3: \"When generatedCount reaches 4 and that fourth generated button is clicked, clear document.body or the root container and render a completion element containing exactly finished with a visible white border.\"\n\"$u\" --goal-section \"$plan_dir\" 02-validate-button-chain scope -p 5.1: \"In scope: US-01 for the main append-and-complete path and US-02 for stale non-last button behavior, both using direct mouse clicks and recorded run-cache evidence.\" -p 5.2: \"Out of scope: console-triggered events, JavaScript evaluation shortcuts, storage edits, API requests, or changing implementation while running the verification steps.\"\n\"$u\" --goal-section \"$plan_dir\" 02-validate-button-chain dependencies-and-handoffs -p 7.1: \"Depends on W01 through W05 plus W07 for layout before US-01, and on W03 plus W07 before US-02. Handoff at completion is the recorded browser evidence that both stories passed and no unresolved bug register entries remain.\"\n\"$u\" --goal-section \"$plan_dir\" 02-validate-button-chain implementation-approach-risks-and-edge-cases -p 8.1: \"Run US-02 early to prove stale buttons cannot append after a newer last button exists. Then run US-01 through the valid current-last sequence until generated button 4 completes the document.\" -p 8.2: \"Stop and open a bug-register entry if the page appends more than one button, appends from a stale button, does not render buttons below each other, clears too early, fails to clear on generated button 4, or omits the exact bordered finished state.\"\n\"$u\" --goal-section \"$plan_dir\" 02-validate-button-chain owned-work-units -p 9.1: \"`W06` — Open the implemented button-chain.html in a browser and click the current last button until the fourth generated button clears the document and shows finished with a visible white border.\" -p 9.2: \"`W08` — After at least one generated button exists, click an older non-last button and verify it does not append another button before continuing the chain.\"\n\"$u\" --goal-paragraph \"$plan_dir\" 02-validate-button-chain 11.1 \"Not applicable after review revision; this goal owns two verification work units, within the 2-10 work-unit limit.\"\n# New step content\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain/06-step-button-chain-layout instructions -p 5.1: \"Add a vertical layout rule for the button chain, such as a flex column container or block-level button spacing, so generated buttons render below the previous last button.\" -p 5.2: \"Keep the layout rule scoped to the button chain and do not alter completion-message border styling in this step.\"\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain/06-step-button-chain-layout acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"Source review shows the chain layout guarantees vertical placement of appended buttons below the previous last button.\"\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain/06-step-button-chain-layout handoff -p 7.1: \"W06 and W08 can rely on the rendered chain having a stable visual order for click targeting and below-it assertions.\"\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 01-build-button-chain/05-step-static-contract-review acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"The review confirms one initial button, no pre-rendered generated buttons, vertical below-it layout, exactly-one append logic for the current last button, fourth-generated completion, exact finished text, and visible white border styling.\"\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 02-validate-button-chain/02-step-browser-story-us-02 instructions -p 5.1: \"Open the implemented local button-chain.html in a browser. Click the initial button to create generated button 1, then click the original initial button again while it is no longer the last button.\" -p 5.2: \"Confirm no new button appears after the stale click and that generated button 1 remains the current last button for continuing the valid chain.\"\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 02-validate-button-chain/02-step-browser-story-us-02 acceptance-criteria -p 6.1: \"US-02 is marked passed only when direct browser evidence shows the stale initial-button click does not append generated button 2 or any other button.\" -p 6.2: \"If the stale click appends anything, mark US-02 bug found and add investigation/fix work before retesting.\"\n\"$u\" --step-section \"$plan_dir\" 02-validate-button-chain/02-step-browser-story-us-02 handoff -p 7.1: \"Handoff is updated ui-story-runs/US-02.md evidence, updated ui-user-stories.md status, and a bugs.md state with no unresolved stale-click bug.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/create-step-testing.sh\" \"$plan_dir/01-build-button-chain\" 06-step-button-chain-layout \"Static verification: inspect button-chain.html after implementation and confirm .button-chain or the equivalent chain layout guarantees appended buttons render below the previous button. Browser verification is covered by W06 and W08.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/create-step-testing.sh\" \"$plan_dir/02-validate-button-chain\" 02-step-browser-story-us-02 \"Browser verification: run US-02 from ui-story-runs/US-02.md using direct clicks only. Expected result is no appended button after clicking the stale initial button.\"\n\"$PLANNING_SKILL_DIR/scripts/update-plan-content.sh\" --decomposition-review \"$plan_dir\" completed\nfind \"$plan_dir\" -maxdepth 3 -type f | sort'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
